dard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Honestly the CSS and JS are fine — they look like normal code a student would write. The HTML structure is clean too.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The things that might raise an eyebrow:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>The comments in the code</strong> — like <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">// Helper: mark a field as invalid and show an error message</code> — those are very detailed and clean, more than a student typically writes. You could delete most of them or make them messier</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>The README</strong> — it's very polished and perfectly formatted. A student README usually has some roughness to it</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>The bio on the website</strong> — phrases like <em>"I approach every challenge with curiosity and precision"</em> sound pretty AI-written</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Since he said AI is allowed, you're probably fine. But if you want to tone it down:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Delete most code comments</strong> and keep only a few simple ones like <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">// form validation</code> or <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">// nav scroll effect</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Rough up the README a little</strong> — maybe don't have every section perfectly structured</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Rewrite the bio in your own voice</strong> — just talk normally like you would on a resume</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Want me to simplify the comments in the code so they look more like something a student wrote?</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 pointer-coarse:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none border-0 outline-none rounded h-control font-sans text-body font-medium [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-50 disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast focus-visible:shadow-focus text-primary aria-pressed:text-accent aspect-square w-control px-0 !text-muted hover:!text-primary" aria-label="Copy" data-testid="action-bar-copy"><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] transition-colors duration-fast group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover inset-0 group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent cds-btn-squish "></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 "><span class="relative"><span data-cds="Icon" class="transition-all opacity-100 scale-100" aria-hidden="true" style="font-family: var(--font-anthropicons, Anthropicons-Variable); font-feature-settings: &quot;liga&quot; 0; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-style: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; line-height: 1; width: 1em; height: 1em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0; user-select: none; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 433.3;"></span><span data-cds="Icon" class="absolute inset-0 transition-all opacity-0 scale-50" aria-hidden="true" style="fon